Hi all,

We're running into an issue on our production Kafka cluster (version 3.9.0,
KRaft mode) where:

   - kafka-topics.sh --list works fine and returns the expected topic list.
   - kafka-topics.sh --create fails / hangs when attempting to create a new
   topic.
   - Consumers are unable to consume from existing topics.

*Environment:*

   - Kafka version: 3.9.0
   - Mode: KRaft (no ZooKeeper)
   - Cluster: [e.g., 3-node KRaft cluster, deployed onKubernetes]
   - Deployment: [StatefulSet / VM / bare metal ]

*Symptoms:*

   - Topic creation command output/error: [paste exact error or "hangs with
   no response" here]
   - Consumer error/log snippet: [paste relevant consumer error here]
   - Controller/broker logs around the time of the issue: [paste relevant
   log lines, especially anything about quorum, leader election, or metadata
   log]

*What we've checked so far:*

   - [e.g., broker connectivity, ACLs/authorizer config, controller quorum
   health, disk space on log dirs]
   - [Add/remove based on what you've actually verified]

*Additional context:*
We recently had a KRaft quorum-related incident on this cluster (metadata
log divergence across controller nodes), so we suspect this may be
connected to controller/quorum health, but wanted to check if this is a
known issue or if others have seen similar behavior.

Any guidance on what else to check, or whether this matches a known bug,
would be appreciated. Happy to share more logs/config if useful.

Thanks,
Bala

